  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5603.01 Certificate of Authority for Agents or Employees",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5603.01 Certificate of Authority for Agents or Employees.\n\n(a) Whenever a request for a motor vehicle record is made by an authorized agent or employee of an entity authorized to receive motor vehicle driver records, pursuant to RSA 260:14, an original, valid certificate of authority shall be on file with the department.\n\n(b) The certificate of authority filed by an agent or employee may be valid for up to a one year period, unless a shorter period of time is set forth by the principal on the certificate of authority or unless revoked by the principal.\n\n(c) If the certificate of authority for an agent or employee is revoked prior to its expiration date, the principal shall be responsible for notifying, in writing, the director of motor vehicles at 23 Hazen Drive, Concord, NH 03305.\n\nSource. #6403, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-97; rpld and ss by #7361, EXEMPT, eff 9-1-00; ss by #7621, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-02; ss by #13152, EXEMPT, eff 12-31-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html"
